  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0089_034c36a63735.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 130px;\" /></p><p>The wire makes an angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;with the magnetic field lines. Therefore, the induced emf will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>sin</mi><msup><mn>45</mn><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p><p><math><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1.1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"
